[{:db/id 17592186321001 :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=5{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}=-2{b}_{1}?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119824 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-52843c58-6ada-5ce6-8fe3-a0a1c897ac6d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-52843c58-6ada-5ce6-8fe3-a0a1c897ac6d" :question/id #uuid "52843c58-6ada-5ce6-8fe3-a0a1c897ac6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-80817" :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=-4{b}_{3}$, ${c}_{2}=5{b}_{1}$ and ${c}_{3}=-3{b}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =8{b}_{1}-2{b}_{2}+3{b}_{3} \\\\  & =3{b}_{3}+8{b}_{1}-2{b}_{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}(-4{b}_{3})+\\frac{8}{5}(5{b}_{1})+\\frac{2}{3}(-3{b}_{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}{c}_{1}+\\frac{8}{5}{c}_{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{c}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ \\frac{8}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5dfb7050-a4fe-5646-9ebf-d0c4cc689423"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5dfb7050-a4fe-5646-9ebf-d0c4cc689423" :answer-field/id #uuid "5dfb7050-a4fe-5646-9ebf-d0c4cc689423" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6a201169-6127-5146-ac33-370dbaeb9fed" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7cf45f1d-e7fe-5ad3-af94-a089a9eeec5f" "answer-6a201169-6127-5146-ac33-370dbaeb9fed" "answer-6d16febb-185e-5f02-b767-d0d169b5dbfe" "answer-eb796ee2-fa6f-5226-9fdb-c601791894cc" "answer-e664d5e6-21e0-5873-967f-9bc8ff95c930"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7cf45f1d-e7fe-5ad3-af94-a089a9eeec5f" :answer/id #uuid "7cf45f1d-e7fe-5ad3-af94-a089a9eeec5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a201169-6127-5146-ac33-370dbaeb9fed" :answer/id #uuid "6a201169-6127-5146-ac33-370dbaeb9fed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ \\frac{8}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d16febb-185e-5f02-b767-d0d169b5dbfe" :answer/id #uuid "6d16febb-185e-5f02-b767-d0d169b5dbfe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb796ee2-fa6f-5226-9fdb-c601791894cc" :answer/id #uuid "eb796ee2-fa6f-5226-9fdb-c601791894cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ \\frac{8}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e664d5e6-21e0-5873-967f-9bc8ff95c930" :answer/id #uuid "e664d5e6-21e0-5873-967f-9bc8ff95c930" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119825 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b0e4cc3b-3144-5373-932e-12723fa2aecf"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b0e4cc3b-3144-5373-932e-12723fa2aecf" :question/id #uuid "b0e4cc3b-3144-5373-932e-12723fa2aecf" :question/math-academy-id "q-112862" :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=2{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}={b}_{1}+{b}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We are given that\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}=2{b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2}={b}_{1}+{b}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the $b$'s in terms of $c$'s. From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n{b}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{c}_{2}={b}_{1}+(\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1})\\,⟹\\,{b}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]$, we can write the vector $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={b}_{1}-5{b}_{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}-5(\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{2}{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\  & =-3{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c70a1919-efd3-511f-9ea6-f55df071b113"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c70a1919-efd3-511f-9ea6-f55df071b113" :answer-field/id #uuid "c70a1919-efd3-511f-9ea6-f55df071b113" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e97d3d12-325a-5425-988a-d90f7923ca9c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e97d3d12-325a-5425-988a-d90f7923ca9c" "answer-c9b65cef-3b11-5aa5-8c39-6a1bd856ef09" "answer-cb6a6cb4-14b9-5dc8-a71d-66abf40eedf6" "answer-3e4d1efa-0b11-5604-b83d-1cafc0e12e97" "answer-e6f678ca-51ca-5faa-80f3-6687002731fd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e97d3d12-325a-5425-988a-d90f7923ca9c" :answer/id #uuid "e97d3d12-325a-5425-988a-d90f7923ca9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c9b65cef-3b11-5aa5-8c39-6a1bd856ef09" :answer/id #uuid "c9b65cef-3b11-5aa5-8c39-6a1bd856ef09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb6a6cb4-14b9-5